<title>BELGIUM: EU 1st tranche sugar output levy seen unchanged.</title>
<headline>EU 1st tranche sugar output levy seen unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The first instalment of the European Union's 1996/97 (July/June) sugar production levy is likely to be unchanged from last season, EU member state officials said.</p>
<p>&quot;This is because the intervention price remains the same,&quot; said one official, commenting on a discussion by the EU sugar management committee on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The first instalment, which is half the annual levy, is fixed as a percentage of the white sugar price.</p>
<p>Last year the first instalment levies  were 0.632 Ecus per 100 kg for &quot;A&quot; quota sugar and 11.848 Ecus per 100 kg for &quot;B&quot; quota.</p>
<p>The inulin syrup &quot;A&quot; quota levy was 0.632 Ecus per 100 kg and its &quot;B&quot; quota was 11.848 Ecus per 100 kg.</p>
<p>The first tranche of the isoglucose levy was 0.506 Ecus per 100 kg.</p>
<p>The levy, paid by sugar processors and growers, is used to finance the cost of subsidised exports to non-EU countries.</p>
<p>-Peter Blackburn,Brussels newsroom 287 6830</p>
